# Jazz Comping: Shell Voicings on ii-V-I (repertoire plan: st-jazz-shells). An original 16-bar
# comping study in C: Dm7 | G7 | Cmaj7 | Cmaj7, four times. Three-note shells, root, third and
# seventh only, on strings 6 to 3:
#   Dm7 (x535xx): D, F, C      G7 (3x34xx): G, F, B      Cmaj7 (x324xx): C, E, B
# Two notes hardly move: F stays put from Dm7 to G7 (string 4 fret 3) and falls to E for Cmaj7;
# C on string 3 falls to B for G7 and stays there for Cmaj7.
# Bars 1-8: four short chords a bar, on every beat. Bars 9-16: the Charleston rhythm, beat 1 and
# the "and" of 2. Swing feel: the "and" is the last third of the beat, written as a triplet
# (a rest of two thirds, then the chord). Muted strings: the fingers touch the strings they do
# not press, and the picking hand strums only the three strings of the shell.
# The teacher walks a bass line in quarter notes, root on beat 1.
title: Jazz Comping: Shell Voicings on ii-V-I
